 ;; ── decision — D1..D6 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 :decision
 {:D1 "Actor COUNT stays 18,342; only hand-written FILES collapse. One functional organism framework + per-code data -> 18,342 living, individuated, functional actors. The 'functional/organic' comes from 4 sources: per-code data, a capability library generalized from the bespoke tier, Murakumo inference, and organism life (heartbeat/joucho)."
  :D2 "Extract kotodama to its OWN repo (etzhayyim/kototama); root references it as a dependency."
  :D3 "kotoba Rust engine (17 crates) = EXTERNAL dependency, not an in-tree submodule; remove the submodule from root."
  :D4 "Split the kotodama runtime off the Step-8 gate; the murakumo runtime rename (220-file atomic) stays out of scope."
  :D5 :invariants ;; the invariants block below is D5
  :D6 "Founder ratification: PR review (Council attestation = PR review)."}

 ;; ── invariants (D5) — fixed by this ADR, must hold post-migration ──────────
 :invariants
 ["18,342 full coverage maintained (= registry totalCount)"
  "every actor FUNCTIONAL — empty-stub forbidden (enforced in code + tests: an empty procurement line is always rejected)"
  "DID invariant: did:web:etzhayyim.com:actor:c<code>"
  "Murakumo-only inference (ADR-2605215000) — build-time data gen via sub-agents is NOT a runtime inference path"
  "kotoba Datom = canonical state (ADR-2605262130 / 2605312345)"
  "Apache-2.0 + Charter Compliance Rider inherited"]

 ;; ── consequences ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 :consequences
 {:positive ["all 18,342 actors gain real, commodity-specific function (stubs eliminated)"
             "18,343 hand-written .py collapse to framework + data"
             "root no longer carries the kotoba submodule (lighter clone/CI)"
             "actor state persists as-of on the kotoba Datom log (organic trajectory)"]
  :risks ["18,342 Murakumo-heartbeat load on the 10-node fleet — mitigated by cadence control + fail-open fallback (ibuki R1 precedent)"
          "enrichment quality drives functional quality — mitigated by the capability library + spec floor + bespoke golden-trace parity"]
  :wiring-to-update ["CLAUDE.md (substrate-engine decl / cell-catalog pointer / do-not rename clause)"
                     "bb.edn test tasks" "50-infra/murakumo/fleet.toml + placement-contract.yaml"
                     "CHARTER-RIDER.md (nv_compat path)" "70-tools/scripts/lint/substrate-boundary.mjs"
                     "PYMAGATAMA-MIGRATION-NOTES.md relocation"]}

 ;; ── alternatives considered (all rejected) ────────────────────────────────
 :alternatives
 [{:option "collapse to ONE parametric stub + delete 16,687" :rejected "still a stub; coverage gains no function (founder: all must be functional/organic)"}
  {:option "vendor the whole kotoba repo into root (in-tree copy)" :rejected "heavy (Rust+py); loses upstream sync"}
  {:option "machine-translate all 1,655 bespoke to individual clj" :rejected "1,655 verification cost; does not lift the 16,687 to functional"}
  {:option "keep the submodule, clj-ify the py in place" :rejected "retains the Step-8 lock + physical embedding; fails the 'no submodule in root' goal"}]

